  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Santosh Vishnu Relekar vs The State Of Maharashtra on 21 February, 2022 Author: C.V. Bhadang Bench: C.V. Bhadang 19-aba-461-2022 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Anticipatory Bail Application No.461 Of 2022 Santosh Vishnu Relekar ...Applicant Vs. The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent ---- Mr.Prioyal G. Sarda for the Applicant. Mr.A.R. Kapadnis, App for the Respondent-State. Digitally signed Nilam by Nilam Santosh ---- Santosh Coram : C.V. Bhadang, J. Kamble Kamble Date: 2022.02.21 17:11:15 +0530 Date : 21 February 2022 P.C. .",
    "facts": "The Applicant, apprehending arrest, in connection with the investigation of Crime No.15 of 2022 registered with Vairag Police Station, under Section 188,272, 273 and 328 of the Indian Penal Code and 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e) and 59 of the Food and Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is seeking anticipatory bail. 2. The aforesaid crime is registered on the basis of t complaint lodged by Ms.Pradnya Surase, Addit Commissioner of Food and Drugs Department, Solapur. The allegations is that in a raid conducted in the agricultural field of Santosh Vishnu Relekar vs The State Of Maharashtra on 21 February, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/182690221/ 1 the Applicant Panmasala/Guthka which is banned has been recovered. The learned counsel for the Applicant states that Section 328 of the IPC is only non-bailable Section and all other Sections are bailable.",
